# short-description: QEMU virtio-blk disk with swupdate dual-copy (A/B) rootfs
# long-description: kernel/devicetree/u-boot are supplied externally via
# QEMU's -kernel/-bios (this board's u-boot doesn't load them from disk,
# see the README), so this disk only needs to carry what swupdate's A/B
# mechanism itself needs: a small "boot" partition holding the
# bootstate-trying.env/bootstate-good.env marker files, two identical
# rootfs copies (rootA active by default), and a small "state" partition
# for the uEnv.txt-equivalent rootpart/bootstate override.
#
# boot and state are vfat, not ext4 -- confirmed real: qemu_arm64_defconfig's
# U-Boot has no CONFIG_CMD_EXT4_WRITE/CONFIG_EXT4_WRITE at all ("Unknown
# command 'ext4write'", and the generic `save` command's ext4 backend
# also fails to write), but does have `fatwrite`. This is the mirror
# image of the real AM335x hardware's own U-Boot, which has ext4write
# but no FAT write command -- the two boards simply differ in which
# write path their U-Boot build enables, so this layout picks whichever
# one is actually real for this target rather than assuming.

part --source bootimg-partition --fstype=vfat --label boot --align 1024 --fixed-size 8M
part / --source rootfs --fstype=ext4 --label rootA --align 1024 --use-uuid --fixed-size 384M
part /rootfs-b --source rootfs --fstype=ext4 --label rootB --align 1024 --use-uuid --fixed-size 384M
part --fstype=vfat --label state --align 1024 --fixed-size 4M
